  "body": "See https://github.com/w3c/mediacapture-fromelement/issues/29\n\nhttp://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-fromelement/ says \"A new frame is requested from the canvas when `frameCaptureRequested` is true and the canvas is painted.\"\n\nThe \"canvas is painted\" bit is not specific enough. I don't know the canvas element very well, but I think what is needed is a concept of when a canvas is committed, presumably at the earliest at a microtask checkpoint following some manipulation of the canvas. A hook at this point could be used by the Media Capture spec.\n\n@martinthomson @Pehrsons @uysalere @junov \n",
